      "tree_id": "959db442cb696ae3f761129d582f3345217368fd",
      "message": "The transcript shows record handles as chips and sets maths apart\n\nA handle in an agent's message whose prefix the domain names (CLM_3,\nEV_4) is rendered as a chip carrying its record type, and is a button\nwhen the host supplies an open handler. Maths such as z_o = mean_{i in o}\nis set in its own span. Text in code or a link is left as written, and a\nhandle inside a formula is part of the formula.\n\nThe rules live in packages/records, apart from React, so the explorer\ncan adopt them when it is ported.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GVjyjkaADPAqLvtnf3xUNs",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-27T00:09:35Z",
